/*
 * Endpoint Name: GetCurrentUserEndpoint
 * HTTP Method: GET
 * Backend Route: /api/auth/me
 * 
 * Future Request Contract: None (uses JWT from Authorization header)
 * 
 * Future Response Contract: CurrentUserResponse
 *   - User: UserDto (current authenticated user profile)
 * 
 * Required Permission: Valid JWT token
 * 
 * Related Domain Entities:
 *   - User (Domain/Entities/User.cs)
 * 
 * Validation Steps:
 *   1. Validate JWT token is present and valid
 *   2. Extract UserId from JWT claims
 *   3. Verify user exists in database
 * 
 * Implementation Steps:
 *   1. Extract UserId from JWT claims (User.FindFirst(ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier))
 *   2. Query User by Id from AppDbContext
 *   3. Check if user exists and is Active
 *   4. Map User entity to UserDto (exclude PasswordHash)
 *   5. Return CurrentUserResponse with user info
 * 
 * Error Cases:
 *   - 401 Unauthorized: missing or invalid JWT token
 *   - 404 Not Found: user not found in database
 *   - 403 Forbidden: user account is suspended or inactive
 *   - 500 Internal Server Error: unexpected database errors
 * 
 * EXPLICIT NOTE: NOT IMPLEMENTED IN PHASE 3C
 * This file is a TODO skeleton only. Real implementation will be done in later phase.
 */

